<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Somalia</h1><p class="st-meta">1991 CE – present · capital Mogadishu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Somali state since the collapse of 1991, rebuilt slowly through transitional governments into a federal republic still fighting al-Shabaab.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siad-barre">Siad Barre</a> fled in January 1991, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/somali-democratic-republic">Somali Democratic Republic</a> collapsed. Rival factions fought over <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-mogadishu">Mogadishu</a>, and famine in 1992 killed hundreds of thousands, prompting UN and US intervention, which ended after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mogadishu-1993">Battle of Mogadishu</a> in 1993. The north became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-somaliland">Republic of Somaliland</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puntland">Puntland</a> formed as an autonomous state in 1998.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transitional-national-government">Transitional National Government</a> formed in 2000 and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transitional-federal-government">Transitional Federal Government</a> in 2004. In 2006 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islamic-courts-union">Islamic Courts Union</a> took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-mogadishu">Mogadishu</a>, provoking Ethiopian intervention, from which the militant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-shabaab">al-Shabaab</a> emerged. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-union">African Union</a> troops of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-union-mission-to-somalia">AMISOM</a>, from 2007, helped push al-Shabaab out of Mogadishu in 2011. A provisional constitution in 2012 created the Federal <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/somali-republic">Republic of Somalia</a> with federal member states.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Somalia remains a federal republic with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-mogadishu">Mogadishu</a> as capital, governed by indirect elections among clan delegates, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-shabaab">al-Shabaab</a> still controls parts of the countryside. Remittances, telecoms and livestock exports sustain the economy.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/somalia.jpg" alt="Somalia" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: see upload history · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Somalia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1991 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mogadishu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abdullahi Yusuf Ahmed, Hassan Sheikh Mohamud, Mohamed Abdullahi Farmaajo</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Somali, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/somalia">Somalia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Federal Republic of Somalia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=2008&amp;focus=somalia" aria-label="Somalia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5939 2101 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Somalia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6259 2357L6259 2357"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6259 2357h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6259 2357h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6259 2357h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mogadishu. <a href="/atlas?year=2008&amp;focus=somalia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
